    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1537">

                <pb facs="0987" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/60.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Saltillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-18T19:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 16, 5 p.m. General Natera, Governor of Zacatecas, at present in
                    Monterey disclaims any knowledge of death and persecution of Christian Brothers.
                    States that Villa would know of the facts <pb facs="0988" n="872" xml:id="pg872"
                    /> in the case. Have made verbal and written representation to Governor Carranza
                    in the matter. Welfare of Christian Brothers at Saltillo reported to Department
                    yesterday.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
